-- KarbonFM demo seed data (owner, 2026-10-28; OD-03-01): invented names and amounts that match design/ ("Carbon & Ember").
-- Apply after 04_database_schema.sql on an empty database:
--   sqlite3 demo.db < 04_database_schema.sql && sqlite3 demo.db < 04_demo_seed.sql
-- Generated by a script, then checked: every balance below follows from the lines, tax and payments.
--
-- What matches design/ exactly:
--   * customers.html: 14 customers (13 current, 1 inactive); balance due $29,619.05; overdue $4,457.40
--     at 3 customers, oldest 41 days on 2026-10-28; retainer balance $4,450.00 held for 4 customers; every per-row balance.
--   * customer.html: Halden & Pryce balance due $3,057.15, retainer balance $1,500.00 (RET-0042 $3,000 - $1,000 applied on
--     INV-1035 - $500 on INV-1048), revenue in the last 12 months $16,370.00, open pipeline $24,500.00, its 6 transactions,
--     3 contacts, 3 opportunities, 4 files and the activities shown.
--   * invoice.html: INV-1048 lines 2 x $1,200.00, $450.00, 6 x $95.00, 4 x $32.50 (taxable); subtotal $3,550.00; tax 5.5%
--     on $130.00 = $7.15; retainer applied $500.00; payment $1,000.00 (Check #2214); balance due $2,057.15.
-- Differences, on purpose:
--   * The plan stores an applied retainer as a negative "Retainer" line (BR-SALES-18), so total_amt is after the credit
--     (INV-1048: $3,057.15, INV-1035: $4,200.00). The mockup shows the amount before the retainer and the credit below it;
--     the balance due is the same.
--   * Dashboard aggregates (October revenue, the 12-month chart, 14 open invoices, 11 opportunities) are illustrative in
--     index.html and are not reproduced; the seed has 9 open invoices and 7 opportunities.
--   * Opportunity stages use the source statuses (607); the mapping is noted at the opportunities.
--   * customers.html says the balance is "across 9 customers", but its rows show 8 customers with a balance; the seed
--     follows the rows (8 customers, 9 open invoices; Halden & Pryce has two, INV-1042 is due Oct 30).
--   * subtotal includes the retainer credit line (INV-1048 subtotal $3,050.00, as BR-SALES-02 sums every line).
--   * Ids are readable text keys (p-hp, t-inv-1048) instead of UUIDs, so the demo is easy to read.
--   * The chat screen (UI-21) is a static template; it needs no rows.

PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;

BEGIN;
-- Reference seeds: the source ids and names (BR-ADMIN-02; D-19: the same ids are Rust enums).

-- The business that owns the install, and its single user (BR-ADMIN-01, BR-ADMIN-04).

-- 14 customers (design/customers.html). Balances are what the transactions below leave open.

-- Items. "Retainer" is the item BR-SALES-07 counts; Apply Retainer adds a negative line of it (BR-SALES-18).

-- Customer rows with their cached balance and retainer balance (recomputed by the commands; BR-SALES-02, BR-SALES-06).

-- Sales transactions, lines and payments. Totals follow BR-SALES-01/02: line amount = qty x unit price (cents);
-- tax = taxable subtotal x tax_rate_bp, rounded half away from zero; balance = total - payments. All are posted (locked_ind = 1).

-- Opportunities. Stages map to the source statuses: Lead -> 1 New, Qualified -> 2 In process, Proposal and Negotiation -> 3 Proposal sent, Won -> 4 Won.

-- Activities on Halden & Pryce, each linked to the customer (Regarding, 63) and to Mara (Creator, 50).

-- Files: rows only. The demo ships no file bodies; container_path names where a copied file would be (D-17).

COMMIT;
